[00:00.44]Lesson 4 | 第4课
[00:02.94]Seeing Hands | 感知之手
[00:09.61]How did Vera discover she had this gift of second sight? | 维拉是怎样发现自己具有“第二视觉”这种天赋的呢？
[00:16.12]Several cases have been reported in Russia recently of people who can read and detect colours with their fingers, and even see through solid doors and walls. | 最近，俄罗斯有报道称，一些人能够用手指阅读文字、辨别颜色，甚至能看穿坚实的门和墙壁。
[00:27.32]One case concerns an 11-year-old schoolgirl Vera Petrova, | 其中一个案例涉及一名11岁的女学生维拉·彼得洛娃。
[00:32.15]who has normal vision but who can also perceive things with different parts of her skin, and through solid walls. | 她的视力正常，但也能用皮肤的不同部位感知事物，甚至能隔着坚实的墙壁感知物体。
[00:40.70]This ability was first noticed by her father. | 她的父亲最先发现了她的这种能力。
[00:44.14]One day she came into his office and happened to put her hands on the door of a locked safe. | 一天，她走进父亲的办公室，恰好把双手放在一个锁着的保险柜门上。
[00:50.44]Suddenly she asked her father why he kept so many old newspapers locked away there, | 突然，她问父亲，为什么要把那么多旧报纸锁在里面，
[00:56.18]and even described the way they were done up in bundles. | 她甚至还描述了那些报纸捆扎成捆的方式。
[01:00.32]Vera's curious talent was brought to the notice of a scientific research institute in the town of Ulyanovsk, near where she lives, | 维拉这种奇特的天赋引起了她居住地附近、乌里扬诺夫斯克市一家科研机构的注意，
[01:09.76]and in April she was given a series of tests by a special commission of the Ministry of Health of the Russian Federal Republic. | 4月，俄罗斯联邦共和国卫生部的一个特别委员会对她进行了一系列测试。
[01:19.54]During these tests she was able to read a newspaper through an opaque screen and, stranger still, | 在这些测试中，她能够隔着不透明的屏障阅读报纸；更奇怪的是，
[01:25.45]by moving her elbow over a child's game of Lotto she was able to describe the figures and colours printed on it; | 她把肘部移过一张儿童乐透游戏卡片，竟然能够说出上面印着的数字和颜色；
[01:32.91]and, in another instance, wearing stockings and slippers, | 还有一次，她穿着长筒袜和拖鞋，
[01:36.72]to make out with her foot the outlines and colours of a picture hidden under a carpet. | 竟然能够用脚辨认出藏在地毯下面的一幅画的轮廓和颜色。
[01:42.69]Other experiments showed that her knees and shoulders had a similar sensitivity. | 其他实验表明，她的膝盖和肩膀也具有类似的感知能力。
[01:48.26]During all these tests Vera was blindfolded; and indeed, except when blindfolded she lacked the ability to perceive things with her skin. | 在所有这些测试中，维拉的眼睛都被蒙住了；事实上，只有在蒙住眼睛时，她才能用皮肤感知事物。
[01:56.86]It was also found that although she could perceive things with her fingers this ability ceased the moment her hands were wet. | 人们还发现，尽管她能用手指感知事物，但双手一旦沾水，这种能力就会消失。